PR #21 — Rule engine and compliance report model
Branch: feat/rule-engine               Depends on: #20               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  Measurements plus spec, in. A typed, ordered, human-readable verdict out —
  where every failure carries a physical action the user can take.

  DECIDED: rule identities follow ISO/IEC 19794-5, which defines 30 face-image
  requirements. Every national specification derives from that standard, so
  adopting its taxonomy makes our vocabulary match the authorities' own
  documentation, makes us directly comparable to the BioLab-ICAO benchmark and
  to BioGaze, and stops us inventing terms nobody else uses. The 17 rules in
  the fidelity matrix become a subset of the 30, each carrying its ISO id.

IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] Rule definitions with an ISO/IEC 19794-5 requirement id, severity,
      confidence and evaluator
  [ ] Coverage map: which of the 30 ISO requirements we check, which we defer
      to a manual checklist, and which we cannot detect — published on the site
      as a credibility signal rather than hidden
  [ ] Verdicts: pass / fail / warning / manual-check / undetectable
  [ ] Fix instructions computed from the delta ("move ~30cm closer")
  [ ] Overall verdict aggregation and rule ordering by importance
  [ ] Manual checklist for glasses, head covering and recency

EDGE CASES
  [ ] Detection failed entirely — must not report "pass" by omission
  [ ] Low-confidence results must degrade to manual-check, never to pass
  [ ] Contradictory rules resolved deterministically
  [ ] Fix instructions must stay correct when two rules interact (moving closer
      fixes head height but may break the eye line)
  [ ] Never emit "guaranteed to pass" anywhere in the model or copy
  [ ] All messages come from the content module — i18n-ready, no literals

SEO  n/a

TESTS
  Unit: every rule, every verdict state, aggregation, message resolution.


