───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PR #27 — Live camera capture with real-time guidance
Branch: feat/camera-capture            Depends on: #26               Status: TODO
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DESCRIPTION
  PULLED FORWARD from v1.1 into v1, on competitive evidence. PhotoAiD's mobile
  apps have this and we would be the only serious tool without it.

  It removes the retake loop entirely, which is the single loudest complaint in
  every competitor's reviews: people upload, get rejected, upload again, and give
  up around the fourth attempt. Live feedback replaces that with "move closer…
  closer… hold there".

  Cheap for what it delivers: getUserMedia plus the geometry engine from #17,
  both of which already exist by this point.

IMPLEMENTS
  [ ] getUserMedia capture with rear/front camera switching
  [ ] Live overlay: head oval guide, real-time head-height percentage, a
      background-uniformity warning before the shutter rather than after
  [ ] Analysis on a throttled frame loop, not per frame — full detection at
      camera rate would melt a mid-range phone
  [ ] Capture at the sensor's full resolution, not the preview's
  [ ] Falls back cleanly to file upload wherever camera access is unavailable

EDGE CASES
  [ ] Permission denied, or dismissed without answering
  [ ] No camera present (most desktops)
  [ ] iOS Safari requires a user gesture and refuses getUserMedia over http
  [ ] Preview resolution far below capture resolution — guidance computed on the
      preview must still hold for the captured frame
  [ ] Device rotation mid-session
  [ ] Front camera mirroring: the preview is mirrored, the capture must not be
  [ ] Battery and thermal cost of a sustained analysis loop
  [ ] Stream must be stopped on unmount, or the camera light stays on — which
      for this product looks exactly like the surveillance we promise we are not
  [ ] Low light, where guidance would be confidently wrong

SEO
  [ ] Camera UI is client-only and must not enter the static HTML of any page

TESTS
  Unit against a mocked MediaStream; the fixture corpus drives the guidance
  logic. Integration with Playwright's fake camera device.

